      "writtenOn": "2022-06-28T14:47:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In Shape, conservativeContains() is allowed to give false negatives (doesn\u0027t think something is contained) but it cannot give false positives. The true containment test for text would be something like checking the point or rect against every glyph\u0027s path, but path conservative contains is only implemented for convex paths. Given glyphs are hardly ever convex, I\u0027d been assuming the clipping code that relies on Shape::conservativeContains() would just assume that text and other geometry like SkVertices never contain anything.",
